, 1968. They strive to be a world class library and information hub.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"National Library Service of Botswana","names":{"fr":"Botswana. National library service","es":"Biblioteca Nacional de Botsuana","ru":"Ботсванская государственная библиотечная служба"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/Palapye_Public_Library_Signboard.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/Palapye_Public_Library_Signboard.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Olgatladi2020","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palapye_Public_Library_Signboard.jpg"}},{"id":"gaborone_botswana_national_stadium","areaId":"gaborone","name":"Botswana National Stadium","category":"other","tags":["family"],"location":{"lat":-24.6568,"lng":25.93289},"visitMinutes":90,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"gaborone_botswana_national_stadium","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":2,"wikiPageviews":535,"wikidataSitelinks":11,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["botswananationalstadium","gaborone"],"summary":"The Botswana National Stadium is a multi-purpose stadium in Gaborone, Botswana. It is currently used mostly for football matches. The stadium holds 25,000 people.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Botswana National Stadium","names":{"nl":"Nationaal Stadion","es":"Estadio Nacional de Botsuana","ja":"ボツワナ・ナショナルスタジアム","zh":"波札那國家體育場"},"photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8a/Botswana_National_Stadium_August_2010.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8a/Botswana_National_Stadium_August_2010.jpg","w":1200,"h":857,"author":"US Army Africa from Vicenza, Italy","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Botswana_National_Stadium_August_2010.jpg"}},{"id":"gaborone_taras_shevchenko_monument_gaborone","areaId":"gaborone","name":"Taras Shevchenko monument, Gaborone","category":"monument","tags":["history","photo"],"location":{"lat":-24.66018,"lng":25.93086},"visitMinutes":30,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"gaborone_taras_shevchenko_monument_gaborone","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":8,"wikiPageviews":8,"wikidataSitelinks":2,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["tarasshevchenkomonumentgaborone","gaborone"],"bestLight":"morning","summary":"Taras Hryhorovych Shevchenko was a Ukrainian poet, writer, artist, public and political figure, folklorist and ethnographer. His literary heritage, in particular the poetry collection Kobzar, is regarded to be the foundation of modern Ukrainian literature and to some degree also of the modern Ukrainian language.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Taras Shevchenko monument, Gaborone","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/%D0%A2._%D0%93._%D0%A8%D0%B5%D0%B2%D1%87%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%BE._%D0%9A%D0%B2%D1%96%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_1859.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/%D0%A2._%D0%93._%D0%A8%D0%B5%D0%B2%D1%87%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%BE._%D0%9A%D0%B2%D1%96%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_1859.jpg","w":1200,"h":1632,"author":"Andrey Denyer","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A2._%D0%93._%D0%A8%D0%B5%D0%B2%D1%87%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%BE._%D0%9A%D0%B2%D1%96%D1%82%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%8C_1859.jpg"}},{"id":"gaborone_university_of_botswana_stadium","areaId":"gaborone","name":"University of Botswana Stadium","category":"other","tags":["family"],"location":{"lat":-24.65511,"lng":25.94057},"visitMinutes":90,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"gaborone_university_of_botswana_stadium","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":67,"wikidataSitelinks":8,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["universityofbotswanastadium","gaborone"],"summary":"University of Botswana Stadium is a multi-use stadium in Gaborone, Botswana, owned by the University of Botswana. It is used mostly for football matches and serves as the home stadium of Uniao Flamengo Santos F.C. The stadium holds 8,500 people.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"University of Botswana Stadium","names":{"nl":"University of Botswana Stadion","es":"Estadio de la Universidad de Botsuana"}},{"id":"gaborone_wv_statue_of_seretse_khama","areaId":"gaborone","name":"Statue of Seretse Khama","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":-24.6581,"lng":25.9118},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"gaborone_wv_statue_of_seretse_khama","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":3,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["statueofseretsekhama","gaborone"],"summary":"Statue of the country's first president.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Gaborone","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Plumeria_Plant.jpg/1280px-Plumeria_Plant.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Plumeria_Plant.jpg/500px-Plumeria_Plant.jpg","w":1200,"h":1600,"author":"Abbie David","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plumeria_Plant.jpg"}},{"id":"gaborone_wv_the_hindu_hall","areaId":"gaborone","name":"The Hindu hall","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":-24.6434,"lng":25.931},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"gaborone_wv_the_hindu_hall","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-22"},"hashtags":["thehinduhall","gaborone"],"summary":"A large [[Hinduism","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Gaborone"},{"id":"gaborone_wv_news_cafe","areaId":"gaborone","name":"News Café","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":-24.6696,"lng":25.9281},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"gaborone_wv_news_cafe","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.newscafe.co.za/","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["newscafe","gaborone"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"06:30","close":"22:30"},{"open":"06:30","close":"22:30"},{"open":"06:30","close":"22:30"},{"open":"06:30","close":"22:30"},{"open":"06:30","close":"22:30"},{"open":"06:30","close":"22:30"},{"open":"06:30","close":"22:30"}]},"summary":"Close to the Mondior Summit, News Café is popular even with outside guests. The menu centres on \"European style\" dishes, but with some interesting twists. The place really shines in the cocktail department. On Friday and Saturday nights, the music is often cranked up loud even though there is no dance floor, so sit outside if you want to make conversation. Staff are young and sometimes inexperienc","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gaborone"},{"id":"gaborone_wv_bull_and_bush","areaId":"gaborone","name":"Bull and Bush","category":"nightlife","tags":["nightlife"],"location":{"lat":-24.6407,"lng":25.9108},"visitMinutes":90,"photoSeed":"gaborone_wv_bull_and_bush","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["bullandbush","gaborone"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"night","summary":"English pub in north part of [Gaborone]. A common ex-pat hangout big-screen TV and pool tables. Friday night is usually for the younger kids, Saturday night for the adults. The food is excellent, especially the pizza and ribs. The last Wednesday of the month is quiz night (or quizzo) where teams compete on trivia for prizes. Monday night is Rib night and well worth a visit!","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gaborone"},{"id":"gaborone_wv_caravela","areaId":"gaborone","name":"Caravela","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":-24.6618,"lng":25.9209},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"gaborone_wv_caravela","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["caravelagaborone","gaborone"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"One of the few suburban house restaurants in the city. Nominally Portuguese menu including a good selection of seafood, and Mozambican beer. The outdoor patio area has a very nice ambiance. Open for dinner 7 nights a week. Food is a little hit and miss, and the prices are in expat territory, but worth giving a try.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gaborone"},{"id":"gaborone_wv_beef_baron","areaId":"gaborone","name":"Beef Baron","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":-24.6408,"lng":25.8772},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"gaborone_wv_beef_baron","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.grandpalm.bw/things-to-do/restaurants","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["beefbaron","gaborone"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Perhaps Gaborone's most expensive restaurant. Serves excellent and huge meat dishes, including some game, but beef is in the ascendancy. Desserts are good also (including the lovely malva pudding). Atmosphere is pretty nice for a hotel restaurant, although there are no windows.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gaborone"},{"id":"gaborone_wv_funyama_holdings_chinese_restaurant","areaId":"gaborone","name":"Funyama Holdings Chinese Restaurant","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":-24.644,"lng":25.9312},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"gaborone_wv_funyama_holdings_chinese_restaurant","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["funyamaholdingschineserestaurant","gaborone"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Authentic and good value Chinese with an extensive menu, including such delights as Crispy Pork Intestines with Hot Dry Chili. Also covers more standard 'beef in black bean sauce' type dishes. The Devil Soup at P10 and the noodle dishes at P30 are particularly good value.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gaborone"},{"id":"gaborone_wv_abyssinia_ethiopian_cafe","areaId":"gaborone","name":"Abyssinia Ethiopian Cafe","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":-24.6774,"lng":25.9347},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"gaborone_wv_abyssinia_ethiopian_cafe","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["abyssiniaethiopiancafe","gaborone"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Botswana's only Ethiopian restaurant. On Fridays through Sundays this cafe serves pretty good injera with all the trimmings for P80. Also does great coffee and is cleaner and quieter than Equatorial Coffee around the corner. Closed evenings Sunday-Thursday.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gaborone"},{"id":"gaborone_wv_gaborone_yacht_club","areaId":"gaborone","name":"Gaborone Yacht Club","category":"nightlife","tags":["nightlife"],"location":{"lat":-24.7079,"lng":25.9063},"visitMinutes":90,"photoSeed":"gaborone_wv_gaborone_yacht_club","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"https://gaboroneyachtclub.weebly.com/","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["gaboroneyachtclub","gaborone"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"night","summary":"Hidden away down a dusty track to the side of Gaborone dam the Yacht Club bar makes a great sun-downer location. Opening hours are limited, simple food available (e.g., steak-burger & chips P45).","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gaborone"},{"id":"gaborone_wv_notwane_club","areaId":"gaborone","name":"Notwane Club","category":"nightlife","tags":["nightlife"],"location":{"lat":-24.6555,"lng":25.9305},"visitMinutes":90,"photoSeed":"gaborone_wv_notwane_club","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["notwaneclub","gaborone"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"},{"open":"18:00","close":"23:59"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"night","summary":"Used mainly to host private or special DJ events such as The Thursdays Hip Hop Night.The event is a great chance to have a taste of local music and drinks on special prices.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Gaborone"}],"sources":["Wikidata (CC0)","Wikimedia Commons (counts; photos credited per file)","Wikipedia (pageviews; summaries CC BY-SA 4.0)","Wikivoyage (listings: hours, prices, descriptions; CC BY-SA 4.0)","OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL): opening hours, fees, websites"]}